{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136388-your-horror-stories","id":1136388,"title":"Your horror stories.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-01T15:08:59-07:00","id":1136388,"title":"Your horror stories.","content":"Seems appropriate given the question of if there's horror in Mage has come up more than once.<br /> <br /> What have we got folks?<br /> <br /> I think one of my worst moments was after managing to get my character kidnapped. He wakes up in a van speeding through the city to an undisclosed location. No problem, I figure I'm strapped into the gurney and the kidnappers aren't, a sudden stop will throw them out of control long enough for me to escape.<br /> <br /> I had a Familiar that could possess machines, so I ordered it to possess the ambulance and slam on the brakes as hard as possible while I readied a spell to undo the straps on the gurney.<br /> <br /> The plan worked like a charm. Too bad I forgot about the traffic all around us and that my familiar was a trickster spirit who thought it would be good fun to throw the situation into as much chaos as possible.<br /> <br /> I think the worst part though is that I was so obsessed with my own safety that I decided it would be better to ignore the busy intersection full of injured people and mangled vehicles in order to escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T03:31:44-07:00","id":1136530,"title":"","content":"Two things that came up in the first chronicle was a mastigos who teleported family members of a pc thyrsus to torabora caverns where she was held captive in her background, just to illustrate the importance of keeping your feelings and family safe from other mages and why shadow name is a must <br /> <br /> The other was a story that a cabal in congo created the hiv virus to counter a local vampire apocalypse, and the virus got out of hand. Most mages treated it like &quot; i cant judge them, i wasnt there&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T04:33:07-07:00","id":1136543,"title":"","content":"Had a Mastigos go from normal university student to murderer in 2 sessions. She used a shotgun to splatter someone's head at point blank<br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> Her only other friend at the time was a Moros, whom she regularly links to telepathically.<br /> <br /> She's wondering if the nature of Moros mages can trivialize matters of life and death - as if dipping into her friend's mind is contaminating her own.<br /> <br /> <br /> There is also an underlying narrative of personal demons she hasn't confronted yet. Things lingering in the corners of your mind lusting after all the things you find most repulsive and unforgivable.<br /> <br /> <br /> It doesn't help that her breaking points have to do with wanton violence and torture. So to go from 0-100 was deeply unsettling. Of course, she's perfectly free to do what she wants, but defining the context for those actions is pretty intriguing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T07:01:09-07:00","id":1136578,"title":"","content":"A moros arrow who has spent his life before and after Awakening as a soldier. He worried that with every Seer or Banisher he put down he was a step closer to being one of them. He was paranoid they were coming for him, but to my knowledge, never did. He actually took the time to get on good terms with the Guardians, because he recognized that if he did go wrong, he'd need someone to help take him down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T21:52:09-07:00","id":1136826,"title":"","content":"Honestly I don't understand why people say that mage has no horror tone or themes. <br /> <br /> Some of the scariest scenes in my mage sessions:<br /> <br /> the summoning of a superna entity from Pandemonium, with exorcist level of shit and hell entering the room and Messing with mage sight with whispers nightmares and voices in the dark. The mastigos then had to bargain with the creature and had to re live all of his inner demons and and feed his desires to him fucking him up in his mind and soul. <br /> <br /> A moros dealing with a dead kid who was abused raped and killed by a school janitor. The kid didn't even realize he was dead and kept on playing in his house messing with objects and people, he was really scary and scared at the same time. Mage decided to avenge him and tracked down the pedophile and killed him. He kept the ghost kid by his side as his creepy ally, and plays with him in creepy scenes where he seems to be speaking to an non existing little kid in the air. Every time the kid intervenes, ghost and creepy shit happens like whispers and objects flying in the air. That's spooky. Basically now the mage has a ghost following him around, his chains and influences are his little toys which the mage carries around. <br /> <br /> The mages had to investigate on weird kidnappings and people tortured and eaten alive, corrupted sympathetic links and weird secret dungeon rooms in seemingly normal people houses. They were starting to understand and learn about an abyssal cult of Rob zombie style proximi who served an abyssal entity called the prince of 10000 leaves. <br /> I cannot forget how scared and uncertain they were as they entered the rooms where space and sympathy was fucked by the taint of the abyss, and they even witnessed a small cthuluh style fragment of black anty reality oozing from the wall. Creepy and scary as fuck. <br /> <br /> Honestly, mage the awakening can be pretty horror. U just have to narrate it as an horror magic game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T23:50:50-07:00","id":1136848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lasombra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1136388-your-horror-stories?p=1136826#post1136826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I don't understand why people say that mage has no horror tone or themes.<br /> <br /> Some of the scariest scenes in my mage sessions:<br /> <br /> A moros dealing with a dead kid who was abused raped and killed by a school janitor. The kid didn't even realize he was dead and kept on playing in his house messing with objects and people, he was really scary and scared at the same time. Mage decided to avenge him and tracked down the pedophile and killed him. He kept the ghost kid by his side as his creepy ally, and plays with him in creepy scenes where he seems to be speaking to an non existing little kid in the air. Every time the kid intervenes, ghost and creepy shit happens like whispers and objects flying in the air. That's spooky. Basically now the mage has a ghost following him around, his chains and influences are his little toys which the mage carries around.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. That example alone is pretty creepy, but the others were good, too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T04:12:38-07:00","id":1136883,"title":"","content":"Mage Sight can offer lots of opportunities for revealing and creepy hallucinations. Here's an excerpt from one of the text RP sessions I run 1 on 1 for my Players. (I make no claims to be a great writer, just wanted to point out some possibilities)<br /> <br /> A novice Mastigos uses Active Mage Sight on entering a seedy underground club run by the Company (transposed from Boston to London for my games benefit):<br /> <i>As you open yourself to the vision, the Devils work is laid bare before you. The air is lousy with enchantment, it hangs thick in the air reminiscent of incense or opium smoke. A shimmering rainbow cloud that subdues a persons restraint, while heightening the senses and subtly driving a person towards joy and pleasure. It hums in time with the deep bass stereo below, hypnotising.<br /> <br /> The club goers around you are swamped in a mess of infernal symbols you cannot begin to understand. An older man across from you bleeds from his eyes while he drinks wine and woo's a younger man, who to you is shackled with black iron around his neck and wrists. The girls snorting strange substances by the sofa have grown silken wings like butterflies, as if to flap away, but are nailed to the floor by iron spikes, cutting clean through their feet. Pinned in place.<br /> <br /> Your haze is interrupted by a thin lipped woman in a black suit, to you it looks like she is wearing mourning garb, a black band on her left arm. The simple cloth weighs more than stars. &quot;Are you sure this is where you are supposed to be?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> In terms of scenes/situations, Mage has plenty of space for classic body horror. Our opening arc featured Abyssal spiders wrought from human flesh, which bred by biting people, over a few days the bite would bulge and turn necrotic, only to burst in a fatal explosion, unleashing a new swarm of flesh spiders. The Conditions system has really helped get my players into the habit of responding to these sort of things like real people rather than jaded DnD adventurers who might just shrug and ask 'are we rolling initiative yet.' I knew I was on to a winner the first time a player asks me &quot;I think my character would be really freaked out by now, perhaps I could take the Shaken condition?&quot;<br /> <br /> On the Hubris as Horror theme, I totally get that, and love it when it comes up. In our previous session a mystical meteorite fell on a London Church streets away from the cabals sanctum, setting the building on fire with parishoners and staff inside. Some the more heroic Cabal members wanted to spring into action and save as many people as possible, but another cautioned them, pointing out that the Cabal could time travel. They decided to take there time and investigate, finding out as much as they could, THEN go back in time to get everyone out the building before the disaster struck.<br /> <br /> However their investigation reveals that the 'meteor' has disappeared, the Souls of all the surviving parishioners were violently ripped out at the point of impact, and the presence of a powerful Time spell on the crash sight forbids any attempt by Time Travellers to mess with what happened. Que something of a breakdown and much soul searching from the cautious mage, as their assumptions about there own powers have condemned all the Sleepers they might have saved. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}